#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:5
#: 93479d700419428bbdbf2f4fe19e1076
msgid "Maxbotix Analog Sonar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:7
#: 1341a256189a450885d0d73a4e2fb3b9
msgid "`XL-Maxbotix-EZ <https://www.maxbotix.com/product-category/xl-maxsonar-ez-products/>`__ line of analog sonars (XL-MaxSonar-EZ0, EZ4 and EZL0) are relatively inexpensive, short range (7m to 10m) range finder primarily designed for indoor use but which has been successfully used outdoors on Copter and Rover.  These are the predecessors to :ref:`I2C sonar <common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:14
#: f93d94f8f4b04e82ae8d72af50c025e3
msgid "The `EZ4 <https://www.maxbotix.com/Ultrasonic_Sensors/MB1240.htm>`__ (recommended) has the narrowest beam providing the best noise resistance while the `EZ0 <https://www.maxbotix.com/Ultrasonic_Sensors/MB1200.htm>`__ has the widest beam and higher sensitivity.  The long range `EZL0 <https://www.maxbotix.com/Ultrasonic_Sensors/MB1260.htm>`__ has the same sensitivity as the EZ0 but a 10m range (as opposed to 7m)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:22
#: ce2e3eb424d946e6afb9c4ad98675f81
msgid "Connecting to the Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:24
#: 1b9698cf6e3e4920bb11a3ac588d3da8
msgid "The sonar should be connected to the Pixhawk's ADC 3.3V port as shown below. The Pixhawk will provide the regulated 5V power supply the sonar requires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:32
#: 83b3fbf1741245a7ac855f644e7f46dc
msgid "Setup through the mission planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:34
#: aba52d989ba74bdbb84d890614093039
msgid "please first connect with the Mission Planner and then open the Config/Tuning >> Full Parameter List page and set the following parameters (example shown if first rangefinder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:38
#: c487be9471b84ae48420d0d9dcd9a1e7
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_PIN<RNGFND1_PIN>` = \"14\" for Pixhawk's ADC 3.3v pin #2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:39
#: d67604ce775442d396b08f814afe16e5
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MAX<RNGFND1_MAX>` = \"7\" (i.e. 7m max range) if using EZ0 or EZ4, \"10\" if using EZL0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:40
#: 7c407c0b6ad145eca7d49032d7856f1f
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_SCALING<RNGFND1_SCALING>` = \"2.04\" (i.e. 7m / 5v) if using EZ0 or EZ4, \"4.08\" (i.e. 10m / 5v) if using EZL0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:41
#: 6f44bacd040d4dcfb6532be1fd068995
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_TYPE<RNGFND1_TYPE>` = “1\" (Analog)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:45
#: d1f075b4d231481e9bd44f850eca63f7
msgid "The Maxbotix analogue rangefinders according to their data sheets output Vcc/1024 volts per centimetre, or 0.488 v/m when supplied with 5v (which the ADC 3.3v port supplies), which translates into 2.04meters per volt. The range is 7.6m according to the datasheet, but analog output is limited to 7m. As we can only read up to 3.3v then that means 6.75m is the furthest it can really measure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:57
#: b586a0288512462c8e4d7c31872ac5dc
msgid "Testing the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog.rst:59
#: d92154ea33624f52803b4fe7b722ebf6
msgid "Distances read by the sensor can be seen in the Mission Planner's Flight Data screen's Status tab. Look closely for \"rangefinder1\"."
msgstr ""
